  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Triangle I is equilateral with side \\(A,\\) perimeter \\(P,\\) area \\(K,\\) and circumradius \\(R\\) (radius of the circumscribed circle). Triangle II is equilateral with side \\(a,\\) perimeter \\(p,\\) area \\(k,\\) and circumradius \\(r.\\) If \\(A\\) is different from \\(a,\\) then:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(P:p=R:r\\) only sometimes"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(P:p=R:r\\) always"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(P:p=K:k\\) only sometimes"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(R:r=K:k\\) always"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(R:r=K:k\\) only sometimes"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For equilateral triangles, \\(P=3A\\) and \\(R=\\frac{A}{\\sqrt3},\\) with analogous formulas for \\(p\\) and \\(r.\\) Therefore \\[ P:p=A:a=R:r \\] for every such pair of triangles.\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "All equilateral triangles are similar",
        "Perimeter and circumradius both scale linearly with side length"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
